From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:28:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Several classes of a subject map are classes, not a
 function

A subject map with several classes (rr:class ex:Person, ex:Student) was
taken for a class given by a function, since Object.keys of the array of
classes has more than one key: "Cannot read properties of undefined
(reading 'predicateObjectMap')" in subjFunctionExecution (RMLTC0007c of
RMLio/rml-test-cases, CSV, JSON, XML). An array of classes is no longer a
function class map. Test: several classes.
---
 src/input-parser/parser.js        | 4 +++-
 tests/multipleClasses/data.csv    | 2 ++
 tests/multipleClasses/mapping.ttl | 8 ++++++++
 tests/test.js                     | 9 +++++++++
 4 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/multipleClasses/data.csv
 create mode 100644 tests/multipleClasses/mapping.ttl

diff --git a/src/input-parser/parser.js b/src/input-parser/parser.js
index 74a1c94..a234f7f 100644
--- a/src/input-parser/parser.js
+++ b/src/input-parser/parser.js
@@ -120,8 +120,10 @@ const iterateFile = async (Parser, data, currObject, prefixes, options) => {
       );
     }
   }
+  // a class given by a function: an object with more than an @id; several classes
+  // (rr:class a, b) are an array of IRIs, not a function
   const functionClassMap =
-    subjectMap.class && Object.keys(subjectMap.class).length > 1
+    subjectMap.class && !Array.isArray(subjectMap.class) && Object.keys(subjectMap.class).length > 1
       ? subjectMap.class
       : undefined;
 
